placeholders such as {port} or {data_dir} are not expanded inside arguments. A restart claim requires an explicit adapter contract that starts the same frozen application from app_root as a dedicated tester-owned process with isolated per-instance scratch, performs the real actions, stops it, starts it again, and observes persisted behavior; a fresh HTTP client or tester-created database does not prove application restart or persistence. If a read-only external target cannot be restarted, require explicit separate external verification and mark that behavior unverified rather than claiming it passed. Check these facts in acceptance and README/file_plan contracts before any programs are authored.\",\n12:  \"projection_fields\": [\n13:   \"title\",\n14:   \"roles\",\n15:   \"features\",\n16:   \"decisions\",\n17:   \"phases\",\n18:   \"acceptance\",\n19:   \"architecture_markdown\",\n20:   \"limits\",\n21:   \"contract_coverage\",\n22:   \"file_plan\"\n23:  ],\n24:  \"file_plan_included\": true,\n25:  \"source_inventory\": [\n26:   \"ARCHITECTURE.md\",\n27:   \"DRAFT.md\",\n28:   \"RESEARCH.md\",\n29:   \"REVISION.md\",\n30:   \"RUNTIME_CONTRACT.md\"\n31:  ]\n32: }","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/milin/2026/软件开发/application-atlas/application-atlas-production-pack/atlas/template-factory/jobs/job_7742b1c124be4c9ab3a0096da5cdd772/attempt-3/blueprint-spec-review-0-bbc43771a1bbbe99-runtime_protocol-v1/input.json, lines 1-32\n1: {\n2:  \"language\": \"zh\",\n3:  \"guidance_file\": null,\n4:  \"revision_file\": \"source/REVISION.md\",\n5:  \"proposal_digest\": \"f190b65275ab7c7136f523ba92aecde7c9392440d7676b070393e62ff9137b58\",\n6:  \"review_rules_version\": \"atlas.current-required-contract.v1\",\n7:  \"projection_digest\": \"0455d982eea1163b8acf784c572f5bf9d61ea7f9d465a252c3a3e37c8b8f08e1\",\n8:  \"review_dimensions\": [\n9:   \"runtime_protocol\"\n10:  ],\n11:  \"focus\": \"Review the complete proposed architecture, features, phases, acceptance cases, and file plan against source/RUNTIME_CONTRACT.md. Block if any promise conflicts with the isolated tester contract: the tester runs in a separate Python or Node image; Python files run directly as python /suite/acceptance/x.py and cwd is not guaranteed to be /suite, so imports must be explicitly correct; app_root is read-only application source; data_dir is only the tester's mutable scratch at /state and is never the application's database; the only shared connection is network. Delivery profiles are exactly python-web, node-web, static-web, or cli. Web cases must exercise the supplied base_url. Start argv values are literal and placeholders such as {port} or {data_dir} are not expanded inside arguments. A restart claim requires an explicit adapter contract that starts the same frozen application from app_root as a dedicated tester-owned process with isolated per-instance scratch, performs the real actions, stops it, starts it again, and observes persisted behavior; a fresh HTTP client or tester-created database does not prove application restart or persistence. If a read-only external target cannot be restarted, require explicit separate external verification and mark that behavior unverified rather than claiming it passed. Check these facts in acceptance and README/file_plan contracts before any programs are authored.\",\n12:  \"projection_fields\": [\n13:   \"title\",\n14:   \"roles\",\n15:   \"features\",\n16:   \"decisions\",\n17:   \"phases\",\n18:   \"acceptance\",\n19:   \"architecture_markdown\",\n20:   \"limits\",\n21:   \"contract_coverage\",\n22:   \"file_plan\"\n23:  ],\n24:  \"file_plan_included\": true,\n25:  \"source_inventory\": [\n26:   \"ARCHITECTURE.md\",\n27:   \"DRAFT.md\",\n28:   \"RESEARCH.md\",\n29:   \"REVISION.md\",\n30:   \"RUNTIME_CONTRACT.md\"\n31:  ]\n32: }"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \"/Users/milin/2026/软件开发/a